From 369950ed9db192f9ad7d02d5d46e23960ce86bae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:54:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 60 fps step 4: tournament and VS loops through the helper

STD_battleTickFrame and VS_tickFrame call modTickStart/modPresent like
the story battle. The render-side state of both overlays is rolled back
around the extra passes (COMBAT_DATA and the fighters' stats, start text
pieces and timers, finisher gauge, intro name letters, the VS select
panels); the effect render scripts run on every pass with their data
area put back and their outside effects on the first pass only, as in
BTL (the copy goes below the arena model, ARENA_TMD_ADDR, through a new
main-executable helper modEfeAreaSave/Restore). The bracket simulation
moves from STD_renderBracket into a late tick; its projectiles and hit
flashes, which draw from their ticks, are replayed on the extra passes
(ModRollbackSet.replay). The finisher chargeup / target cursor remove
themselves after the passes.

